        -:  544:        uses "const char*" for the third parameter and so can't be used and the
        -:  545:        correct, XPG5, one. Unfortunately we can't just define _XOPEN_SOURCE
        -:  546:        high enough to get XPG5 version as this undefines other symbols which
        -:  547:        make other functions we use unavailable (see <standards.h> for gory
        -:  548:        details). So just declare the XPG5 version ourselves, we're extremely
        -:  549:        unlikely to ever be compiled on a system without it. But if we ever do,
        -:  550:        a configure test would need to be added for it (and _MIPS_SYMBOL_PRESENT
        -:  551:        should be used to check for its presence during run-time, i.e. it would
        -:  552:        probably be simpler to just always use our own wxCRT_StrftimeW() below
        -:  553:        if it does ever become a problem).
